":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T19:04:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T19:04:56Z","body":"While testing this PR, I noticed that in the ProjectSettings or EditorSettings window, the left panel was already snaps to the edge. This behavior doesn't seem intentional — is that expected?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877647432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877700743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-2877700743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":2877700743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rhjqH","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T19:26:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T19:26:36Z","body":"Also it's possible to hide center panel, this is definitely not intended 😄","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877700743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2878259850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-2878259850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":2878259850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rjsKK","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-14T00:25:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-14T00:25:54Z","body":"Made some changes based on the comments:\r\n\r\n- Instead of trying to infer snapping from the splitter position (split offset) the code now uses an explicit snap state. The snap state can be set programmatically (this also allows saving the snap state as part of the editor layout).\r\n- Autosnapping updates the snap state based on the flags like before (i changed the constant names to reflect that they're used for both autosnap setting and the snap state).\r\n- A signal is emitted whenever the snap state changes.\r\n- The dragging state of the dragger is reset when a property (e.g. collapsed) is set to a value that causes dragging impossible while dragging (this was an existing bug that i found while trying to implement the other stuff).\r\n- For the bottom button panel when dragging ends that would end up in a snapped position, the snapping is reset and instead:\r\n  - When trying to snap at the bottom of the screen, the panel collapses its (as if someone clicked on the active button)\r\n  - When trying to snap at the top of the screen, the editor enters in distraction free mode\r\n- The snapping state for the dock splits is now stored in the current editor layout. The default layout is updated with snapping disabled (so someone selecting to restore the default layout with snapped dock splitters will have these splitters unsnapped).\r\n\r\nFor the bottom button panel i tried to have it enter in the collapsed mode automatically *while* dragging but because the buttons themselves are inside the splitter and collapsing it causes all sorts of other side effects the code was becoming way too gnarly for something that seems like a very special case, so instead i made the bottom panel collapse *after* the drag finishes (the effect is almost the same, except you can drag the splitter all the way to the bottom but once you release the mouse button the buttons \"pop\" back out). To make this happen while dragging it'd require moving the buttons outside the splitter, but this felt like a much more intrusive change to me.\r\n\r\nAlso note that while the default setting is to allow autosnapping for both children, this can be changed in cases where autosnapping needs to be done only for one child or disabled. However i think having the default be to autosnap for both is more useful as it'd allow pretty much every splitter to snap and save screen real estate across the editor without any changes (it does cause the unit tests for dragging to fail though so i'll need to see what to do with that).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2878259850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910083078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-2910083078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":2910083078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tdFgG","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T15:18:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T15:18:58Z","body":"Using FIRST/SECOND as snap target will conflict with #90411\r\nNot sure how to handle that though, ideally the other PR should be merged first, but it may take a while 🙃","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910083078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910171071","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-2910171071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":2910171071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tda-_","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T15:59:49Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T15:59:49Z","body":"Btw the title of this commit is far too long, the commit description and title should be brief and clear","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910171071/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3179299219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-3179299219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":3179299219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69gEGT","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T13:15:28Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T13:18:56Z","body":"I’ve already implemented and tested a similar feature [here](https://github.com/blazium-engine/blazium/blob/blazium-dev/scene/gui/split_container.cpp) called `CollapseMode` (in another fork), which also includes RTL layout support. Feel free to reference or adapt any parts that might be useful.\r\nI haven’t opened a separate PR for it, as I’d like to avoid overlap with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90411. We can revisit or merge approaches once we know the direction that PR will take.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3179299219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3179376152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106323#issuecomment-3179376152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106323","id":3179376152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69gW4Y","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T13:36:33Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T13:49:50Z","body":"> Using FIRST/SECOND as snap target will conflict with #90411 Not sure how to handle that though, ideally the other PR should be merged first, but it may take a while 🙃\r\n\r\nCurrently, `SplitContainer` is limited to two children and doesn’t allow dragging the splitter to fully collapse one of them.\r\nThere’s also an open PR proposing a new approach where `SplitContainer` can handle multiple children. However, combining both features in the same node could be complicated.\r\n\r\nOne possible solution would be to deprecate `SplitContainer` in favor of a new node, `SplitDragger`, which could be placed inside a `BoxContainer` between any two children.\r\n`SplitDragger` would act as a resizable divider, letting users drag to adjust the size of the children before and after it, and optionally collapse them completely.\r\nThis way, the resizing logic becomes modular, and we avoid overcomplicating `SplitContainer` while still supporting multiple children and collapsible panels.\r\n\r\nNote: This can Complicate `BoxContainer` and we may consider Adding a new Container for it ie. `SplitterContainer` to avoid breaking compatibility for the original `SplitContainer` node or we solve this issue while upgrading the projects and we add a `SplitDragger` manually for each `SplitContainer`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3179376152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]